2. **Log-concavity check**:
   - Initial check: check if $h'(x_1) \ge h'(x_2) \ge \dots \ge h'(x_k)$.
   - Dynamic check during sampling: when candidate point $x^*$ is evaluated during rejection step and added to $T_k$, insert $x^*$, evaluate $h'(x^*)$, and verify log-concavity across all points in $T_k$. If $h'(x_i) < h'(x_{i+1}) - \text{tol}$, throw error.

3. **Known Distribution Testing (`test()`)**:
